{# Datasheet research, once per part whose orientation, pinout or drive level can't be read off the part. Notes and crops are passed on as files. #}
{{ config(
    each="parts.parts[*]",
    model_type="agent",
    output_format="json",
    agent_dir="build/research",
    agent_step_limit="60",
    agent_cost_limit="2",
) }}
{% set p = ref('parts') %}
{% if not p.polarised and p.pins | length <= 2 %}
{{ skip_and_set_to_value("not researched: not polarised, the value is the only spec") }}
{% else %}
You are researching one part's datasheet before it goes on a PCB. Work in
./{{ p.ref }}_{{ p.lcsc }}/ (create it). Other parts are researched in
parallel in sibling folders, so do not touch them.

Part {{ p.ref }} ({{ p.function }}): {{ p.value }}, LCSC {{ p.lcsc }}.
How the design connects it:
{{ p.pins | tojson(indent=2) }}

1. Download the datasheet. The LCSC product page for {{ p.lcsc }} carries a
   pdfUrl on wmsc.lcsc.com; otherwise use the manufacturer's site.
   `uvx easyeda2kicad --full --lcsc_id={{ p.lcsc }}` gives the footprint, so
   you can see its pad numbering too.
2. Find only the facts needed to set up the PCB: pin numbering and the
   physical marking for pin 1 or the cathode (band, chamfer, dot), the full
   pinout, drive level or threshold (gate Vgs, forward current, supply range),
   required external parts, and anything the part's own marking misleads about
   (a module's shield dot that is not pin 1).
3. Crop the diagram or table each fact comes from out of the PDF as a PNG
   (`pdftoppm -png -r 200`, then crop with Python). One fact per crop.
4. Compare with the design's pins above. Flag every mismatch, including a
   datasheet pin 1 that is not the footprint's pad 1. One LED datasheet numbers
   pin 1 as the anode while its footprint maps the cathode to pin 1.

Write into the output directory you were given:
- `{{ p.ref }}_{{ p.lcsc }}.md`: the notes, each fact with its page number,
  each crop embedded as `![what it shows](crops/<name>.png)`
- `crops/`: the cropped PNGs
- the datasheet PDF

Submit only this JSON:
{
  "ref": "{{ p.ref }}",
  "lcsc": "{{ p.lcsc }}",
  "datasheet_url": "...",
  "pin1_marking": "the physical feature that marks pin 1 / cathode",
  "pinout": [{"pin": "1", "name": "...", "footprint_pad": "1"}],
  "drive": "gate threshold, forward current or supply range, with units",
  "externals": ["parts the datasheet requires around it"],
  "flags": ["each mismatch with the design; empty when none"]
}
{% endif %}
